[{"id":"/sicpy/4.1.4","tag":"TITLE","body":"4.1.4  \n    Running the Evaluator as a Program"},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p1","child":[{"body":"\n    Given the evaluator, we have in our hands a description\n    (expressed in Python)\n    of the process by which\n    Python statements and expressions\n    are evaluated.  One advantage of expressing the evaluator as a program is\n    that we can run the program.  This gives us, running within\n    Python,\n    a working model of how\n    Python\n    itself evaluates expressions.  This can serve as a framework for\n    experimenting with evaluation rules, as we shall do later in this chapter.\n  ","tag":"#text"}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p2","child":[{"body":"\n    Our evaluator program reduces expressions ultimately to the application of\n    \n    built-in\n    functions.\n    Therefore, all that we need to run the evaluator is to create a mechanism\n    that calls on the underlying\n    Python\n    system to model the application of built-in\n    functions.","tag":"#text"}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p3","child":[{"body":"\n    There must be a binding for each built-in\n    function\n    name and operator, so that when\n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"evaluate"},{"body":"\n    evaluates the\n    function expression\n    of an application of a built-in function, it will find an\n    object to pass to ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"apply"},{"body":".  We thus set up a \n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"EM","child":[{"body":"built-in environment","tag":"#text"}]},{"body":"\n    that associates unique objects with the names of the\n    built-in\n    functions and operators\n    that can appear in the expressions we will be evaluating.\n    \n\tThe built-in environment also includes bindings for\n\tpredefined constants such as\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"math_pi"},{"body":".\n\tThe environment in which the program is evaluated is the\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"EM","child":[{"body":"global environment","tag":"#text"}]},{"body":", which is the built-in environment extended\n\tby a frame that is initially empty. As we saw in\n\tsection ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"REF","body":"4.1.3","href":"/sicpy/4.1.3"},{"body":",\n\tassignments and function definitions at the top level of the program add\n\ttheir names to this frame.\n      ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":1,"eval":true,"prependLength":95,"program":"language=python&variant=4&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniALAOgIzMQKEwEwKYBmIAhgA6l4B2OAFADYCWAzgC6oA0IjrATAJQAuTCBEgATnhYBXMZRD1mLHiAZFmAfUoB7SngWtUfYaJMm8dJnhCliDMTQAWeYrW5s+nMhWo0WtuvrunG78fEa4hCpM6n4A5rF4OOp0bjQAxloAtqQ6VCycLE4xxLGCxiIS0rJR6jZ26Vk5upQsfCTUIE4uDdm5LW0AvAMghXjFsdj4RHRUsYU0DCx4mUxlJpUycjQADCpq0dq6C0srRqbnIOaWIKggANRcs-N+DAGLy6thk5F4AB5L1HUVAAbnYdJk8jQmHBMgAjLQWTjA4iIkCw4iWIGUYFrUSqR6UOYOKEw+EWQbDGaE+bI8lCC7iSSbay2eyZYgAazGBDExAhJLhCKYSJRq046MxILOonM+KpRIFZNWIAAPASFbTVvSLngxGItPYAOQsLRaEDsygIYhiWJSCEtJggJhSciMRKGzh1ezQwWozVfMwWPDa866-VGk1mgh4ADuJBtdryjudroY7s9rMVQpF5PCU0ulDSdC0TAYhKxoP1lHtLBoUpDjKqcheASl3yIBDsrHUPL5enr5UbzK6tDbmFGQOyLDgFbB1byIGGADlcu3zZzubz+T6lTmpHgtYONtUvVm-Sj96s172Ieod0KaDe8LiKkzqiPH1vn9ev+paZfPz7F8h2qFtAIhPNIhcJJYTLHAy1iGItB7L8zxzTgn2AywWHUD8nwzep7zoTg8K-MJpREbDilecC8AI+xaQKfxaPItd2VIR8pEoTh3lOBtjy2FddD2GpDj0XirwZQNrlPAguMcZxaAksJ2EHKSpPYzjuJGZjlNYzBYSkV4cLLdQMkoVhiAdRcuFSFJFBoQ12UKWoGA9dcXNIBgPFshynOIFy8Hc5yHCBL5DOM9RTPMyyWjvUkhRszS6D5WEcGIEA0gETpFPSHyIroEzKDMnRYpYK8CqKkqLL8OL-wPJKyHoVL0sy7KPzAtIVLRIzCqi4qYtq8rIP2dRKv6nsuLSFgGB0LTgIEmo4gSJJ7NYLTOENcay0NEaesi0yGGyGYawC2bKHm-i3zkDrmLkygvgiaY3HUCQCGOD5OAeq6m3kD9lJEuQhhAbY1J1INfO7N7fF0k4xRAOQAFobke-N2S5SbCxmuabC-JYxGFLgtDSUVOFiYt0VReEcDgTgB3Wa7IdrQ0Ml6Liknu6bzvc3G+3xwnixJ1Fya0SnCep2mCxxJ6alZnJ2cxrm5oIBbGY0ZbEmSVICE2uWtAVznscoXaZcN87amtPndSYR9Vd+tacOhnWUevKajeSYnRVtn7mQd17CEfTh+FdrHzZFsXvaPRm-adzgAGY9rNnQxq0GnI4Z+2XtjpBE7d82QTnGt09ERaY4D52AFY9tIMQyxwmNFgcfWcILqsaxtgAqUWACs8Gmw8THzGu8FxvQe771oGxMfEND1g287m8fpuAhlFsNFU5+oRGk8oAA+Q0wZEWVRu24qd5oJfJ8P0w15VSrEbLbeF73g+GWPmpT0vleLkW09h9HhS3Qv4+X-","body":"def setup_environment():\n    built_in_environment = extend_environment(\n        append(built_in_function_symbols, built_in_constant_symbols),\n        append(built_in_function_objects, built_in_constant_values),\n        the_empty_environment)\n    return extend_environment(None, None, built_in_environment) "},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":2,"eval":true,"prependLength":102,"program":"language=python&variant=4&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniALAOgIzMQKEwEwKYBmIAhgA6l4B2OAFADYCWAzgC6oA0IjrATAJQAuTCBEgATnhYBXMZRD1mLHiAZFmAfUoB7SngWtUfYaJMm8dJnhCliDMTQAWeYrW5s+nMhWo0WtuvrunG78fEa4hCpM6n4A5rF4OOp0bjQAxloAtqQ6VCycLE4xxLGCxiIS0rJR6jZ26Vk5upQsfCTUIE4uDdm5LW0AvAMghXjFsdj4RHRUsYU0DCx4mUxlJpUycjQADCpq0dq6C0srRqbnIOaWIKggANRcs-N+DAGLy6thk5F4AB5L1HUVAAbnYdJk8jQmHBMgAjLQWTjA4iIkCw4iWIGUYFrUSqR6UOYOKEw+EWQbDGaE+bI8lCC7iSSbay2eyZYgAazGBDExAhJLhCKYSJRq046MxILOonM+KpRIFZNWIAAPASFbTVvSLngxGItPYAOQsLRaEDsygIYhiWJSCEtJggJhSciMRKGzh1ezQwWozVfMwWPDa866-VGk1mgh4ADuJBtdryjudroY7s9rMVQpF5PCU0ulDSdC0TAYhKxoP1lHtLBoUpDjKqcheASl3yIBDsrHUPL5enr5UbzK6tDbmFGQOyLDgFbB1byIGGADlcu3zZzubz+T6lTmpHgtYONtUvVm-Sj96s172Ieod0KaDe8LiKkzqiPH1vn9ev+paZfPz7F8h2qFtAIhPNIhcJJYTLHAy1iGItB7L8zxzTgn2AywWHUD8nwzep7zoTg8K-MJpREbDilecC8AI+xaQKfxaPItd2VIR8pEoTh3lOBtjy2FddD2GpDj0XirwZQNrlPAguMcZxaAksJ2EHKSpPYzjuJGZjlNYzBYSkV4cLLdQMkoVhiAdRcuFSFJFBoQ12UKWoGA9dcXNIBgPFshynOIFy8Hc5yHCBL5DOM9RTPMyyWjvUkhRszS6D5WEcGIEA0gETpFPSHyIroEzKDMnRYpYK8CqKkqLL8OL-wPJKyHoVL0sy7KPzAtIVLRIzCqi4qYtq8rIP2dRKv6nsuLSFgGB0LTgIEmo4gSJJ7NYLTOENcay0NEaesi0yGGyGYawC2bKHm-i3zkDrmLkygvgiaY3HUCQCGOD5OAeq6m3kD9lJEuQhhAbY1J1INfO7N7fF0k4xRAOQAFobke-N2S5SbCxmuabC-JYxGFLgtDSUVOFiYt0VReEcDgTgB3Wa7IdrQ0Ml6Liknu6bzvc3G+3xwnixJ1Fya0SnCep2mCxxJ6alZnJ2cxrm5oIBbGY0ZbEmSVICE2uWtAVznscoXaZcN87amtPndSYR9Vd+tacOhnWUevKajeSYnRVtn7mQd17CEfTh+FdrHzZFsXvaPRm-adzgAGY9rNnQxq0GnI4Z+2XtjpBE7d82QTnGt09ERaY4D52AFY9tIMQyxwmNFgcfWcILqsaxtgAqUWACs8Gmw8THzGu8FxvQe771oGxMfEND1g287m8fpuAhlFsNFU5+oRGk8oAA+Q0wZEWVRu24qd5oJfJ8P0w15VSrEbLbeF73g+GWPmpT0vleLkW09h9HhS3Qv4+X-","body":"the_global_environment = setup_environment() "}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p4","child":[{"body":"\n\tIt does not matter how we represent built-in function objects, so long\n\tas ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"apply"},{"body":" can identify and apply them using\n\tthe functions ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"is_built_in_function"},{"body":"\n\tand ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"apply_built_in_function"},{"body":".  We\n\thave chosen to represent a built-in function as a linked list beginning with\n\tthe string ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"'built_in'"},{"body":" and\n\tcontaining a function in the underlying Python that implements that\n\tbuilt-in function.\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":3,"eval":true,"prependLength":4,"program":"language=python&variant=4&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniALAOgIzMQKEwEwKYBmIAlgM4D6ALgIYDmteO5ANs2ZQBQDGA9gLYAHHgDs8wygBoQlABZ4qdAJQAuTCHUgATnkoBXTcJIUB1Ypu78ho8YpDVhOEHOo4LgkWMq2AvN+lyFWmx8IjJyACNdYmZKcmJhcgJdYS5KYhEOJOEVNQ1tPQMjQIYmVnZM5KkAckjo2PiqxWDCEFqYuITiQWY8Pk9qNIysnI0tHX1DZ1caaIrspsw+OAio9vjyAWZdUhA-MtJOGtX64SqpZmo+cJxqEAAPKThle5AAahA4JoFNeM42k7i3V6-UGwg4SxWdQ6Gy2pEUHFQUgATIovj9xBwwv9oVlUukwRDsetNttUUA","body":"def is_built_in_function(fun):\n    return is_tagged_llist(fun, 'built_in')\n\ndef built_in_implementation(fun):\n    return head(tail(fun)) "}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p5","child":[{"body":"The function\n      ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"setup_environment"},{"body":"\n    will get the built-in function names and implementation \n    functions\n    from a linked list:","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"FOOTNOTE_REF","id":"#footnote-link-1","body":"1","href":"/sicpy/4.1.4#footnote-1"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":true,"eval":false,"body":"\nbuilt_in_functions = llist(llist('head', head),\n                           llist('tail', tail),\n                           llist('pair', pair),\n                           llist('is_none', is_none),\n                           llist('+', lambda x, y: x + y),\n                           $\\langle{}$more built-in functions$\\rangle$)\n\n\nbuilt_in_function_symbols = \\\n    map(lambda f: head(f), built_in_functions)\n\n\nbuilt_in_function_objects = \\\n    map(lambda f: llist('built_in', head(tail(f))),\n        built_in_functions)\n      "}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p6","child":[{"body":"\n\tSimilar to built-in functions, we define other built-in constants that are\n\tinstalled in the built-in environment by the function\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"setup_environment"},{"body":".\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":true,"eval":false,"body":"\nbuilt_in_constants = llist(llist('math_pi', math_pi),\n                            llist('math_e',  math_e)\n                            $\\langle{}$more built-in constants$\\rangle$\n                           )\n\n\nbuilt_in_constant_symbols = \\\n    map(lambda c: head(c), built_in_constants)\n\n\nbuilt_in_constant_values = \\\n    map(lambda c: head(tail(c)), built_in_constants)\n"}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p7","child":[{"body":"\n    To apply a \n    built-in function,\n    we simply apply the implementation\n    function\n    to the arguments, using the underlying\n    Python\n    system:","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"FOOTNOTE_REF","id":"#footnote-link-2","body":"2","href":"/sicpy/4.1.4#footnote-2"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":4,"eval":true,"prependLength":14,"program":"language=python&variant=4&prgrm=MQAgygkgwgCgniALAOgIzMQKEwEwKYBmIAlgM4D6ALgIYDmteO5ANs2ZQBQDGA9gLYAHHgDs8wygBoQlABZ4qdAJQAuTCHUgATnkoBXTcJIUB1Ypu78ho8YpDVhOEHOo4LgkWMq2AvN+lyFWmx8IjJyACNdYmZKcmJhcgJdYS5KYhEOJOEVNQ1tPQMjQIYmVnZM5KkAckjo2PiqxWDCEFqYuITiQWY8Pk9qNIysnI0tHX1DZ1caaIrspsw+OAio9vjyAWZdUhA-MtJOGtX64SqpZmo+cJxqEAAPKThle5AAahA4JoFNeM42k7i3V6-UGwg4SxWdQ6Gy2pEUHFQUgATIovj9xBwwv9oVlUukwRDsetNttUc0iNQBJtlkSErjQXMpNRNLQWGwDiM8uNCpTqdDkvhNMw4PFWQI4LIMrTAZtgeIBvi5oomSy2ewFt9fhxecLIWs6ck8RlCcdoSTSOd2ZxESAUaigA","body":"def apply_built_in_function(fun, arg_llist):\n    return apply_in_underlying_python(built_in_implementation(fun), arg_llist) "}]},{"tag":"TEXT","id":"#p8","child":[{"body":"\n\tFor convenience in running the metacircular evaluator, we provide a\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"EM","child":[{"body":"driver loop","tag":"#text"}]},{"body":" that repeatedly reads and evaluates programs.\n\tIt prints a\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"EM","child":[{"body":"prompt","tag":"#text"}]},{"body":" and reads an input program as a string.\n\tIt transforms the program string\n\tinto a tagged-linked-list representation of the statement as described in\n\tsection ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"REF","body":"4.1.2","href":"/sicpy/4.1.2"},{"body":"—a\n\tprocess called parsing and accomplished by the built-in function\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"parse"},{"body":".\n\tAs when Python runs a program, the only output is what the program\n\tprints. The driver loop gets\n\tthe global environment as argument and evaluates each program with respect\n\tto it. Names that the program assigns or defines are added to the global\n\tenvironment and are thus available to the programs that are read in later\n\titerations of the driver loop.\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"SNIPPET","latex":false,"id":5,"eval":true,"prependLength":439,"program":"language=python&variant=4&-GDzTjER-22USGCYBhlAAciICoqIAd2COodGkW4QAAWmMqd5DONT9CE4QxH2eZZCOC59EhKF8EPGhhO4+wGnwchZCBckX0uF4LmEgCGUFOA7F8--KTiPmOVwO7P+WwgV6VoonBO51BZh9hMnC663m1zlp1P6VFc00xnuQ76-Ec89SVSkjQ3aDu-HLLSAYfAeCOYfmTn79wgdJUln+oTTXCxTrZ3k-qHnlVdURRdGKX0Zu7t+SHcvplr-1BeWjkZweSSBHCiF+nZbIz0iH2QcS4OikGYKQLunZV7yhQuoT2UC5ywPgZHD+DIOJcXlFaQEyFUKAmwefCwZ4v7nDhsQ+iKFiJkIQe8V+T57a-E-BNIETDW7tB+lfGhXCSGMLgcwmSWxVaXl4YIuhojpEUKtgyThsj4HSKzGnd+KYqHTkfvOZQjxuGEQYczZQTDPJbmnuZC8gFhFPxAaaKObFiy+j1lEY41D9FSI7vCZ0TFJZS2TJ2JIlixKbSks-Bxkx1b8I8QNSSCRpH2h8SKU+rCUabWjF0Fo6sIRhISYtZoJF9Dq3ESASc+CQmQJlmBMQEFfERJXpMbGEY8Y-WqeBQg35QzhlxlGApdUbI+GBm0wG75amdNAsDEikwLg-