,"id":"#ex-4.10","child":[{"body":"\n\tEva Lu Ator and Louis Reasoner are each experimenting with the\n\tmetacircular evaluator.  Eva types in the definition of\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"map"},{"body":", and runs some test programs that use it.\n\tThey work fine.  Louis, in contrast, has installed the underlying\n\tversion of ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"map"},{"body":" as a built-in function for\n\tthe metacircular evaluator.  When he tries it, things go terribly wrong.\n\tExplain why Louis's ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"map"},{"body":" fails even\n\tthough Eva's works.\n      ","tag":"#text"}]},{"tag":"DISPLAYFOOTNOTE","id":"#footnote-1","count":1,"href":"/sicpy/4.1.4#footnote-link-1","child":[{"body":"Any\n    function\n    defined in the underlying\n    Python\n    can be used as a built-in function for the metacircular evaluator.  The name of a\n    built-in function installed in the evaluator need not be the same as the name of its\n    implementation in the underlying\n    Python\n    the names are the same here because the metacircular evaluator implements\n    Python    \n    itself.\n    Thus, for example, we could put \n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"llist('first', head)"},{"body":" \n    or \n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"llist('square', lambda x: x * x)"},{"body":"\n    in the linked list of \n    ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"built_in_functions"},{"body":".\n      ","tag":"#text"}]},{"tag":"DISPLAYFOOTNOTE","id":"#footnote-2","count":2,"href":"/sicpy/4.1.4#footnote-link-2","child":[{"body":"\n\tThe function ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"apply_in_underlying_python"},{"body":"\n\tis a built-in function of the language that applies a given\n\tfunction to the elements of a given linked list, which serve as the arguments.\n\tWe also made use of\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"apply_in_underlying_python"},{"body":"\n\tto define the function\n\t","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"PYTHONINLINE","body":"apply_generic"},{"body":"\n\tin section ","tag":"#text"},{"tag":"REF","body":"2.4.3","href":"/sicpy/2.4.3"},{"body":".\n      ","tag":"#text"}]}]